description:
This is partially addressing #279, implementing methods for the Group "Complex" generics. The complex methods I think are a net-win.

I did not include methods for the Group "Summary" generics in this PR because I had second thoughts about if implementing them is a good idea for these reasons:

+  the meaning of `...` would be different between the base R function and the method for tensors.
+  All of these functions are already neatly accessible from the keras backend functions `k_max k_min` etc..

My initial motivation for wanting Summary generics was because it would allow me to write one code path in functions that can take either tensors or R objects as arguments (without coercing everything to a tensor), but now I'm also second guessing if that's even a good idea, or if it will lead to code that's brittle and difficult to reason about. For the record, I was imagining something like this:

```R
#' @export
max.tensorflow.tensor <- function(x, ...) {
  tf$reduce_max(x, ...)
}

#' @export
min.tensorflow.tensor <- function(x, ...) {
  tf$reduce_min(x, ...)
}

#' @export
all.tensorflow.tensor <- function(x, ...) {
  tf$reduce_all(x, ...)
}

#' @export
any.tensorflow.tensor <- function(x, ...) {
  tf$reduce_any(x, ...)
}

#' @export
sum.tensorflow.tensor <- function(x, ...) {
  tf$reduce_sum(x, ...)
}

#' @export
prod.tensorflow.tensor <- function(x, ...) {
  tf$reduce_prod(x, ...)
}

#' @export
range.tensorflow.tensor <- function(x, ...) {
  tf$stack(list(min(x, ...), max(x, ...)))
}
```

Let me know what your thoughts are about implementing the Summary generics and I'll submit a separate PR if you think they're a good idea.

Tensorboard shipped with TensorBoard v1.3 doesn't write a newline at the end of it's output and as a result p$read_output_lines() hangs. This works around that issue by using http to poll for availability of tensorboard.

Tested on Mac, Windows, and Ubuntu with TF v1.2 and 1.3

@kevinushey Could you review this before we merge it?
